{"snapshot":{"pullRequest":{"owner":"KhaiStimpson","name":"andrew-crm","number":58},"title":"Contact data enrichment: external data into fields, AI context, and signals","author":"KhaiStimpson","state":"open","baseRef":"dev","headRef":"claude/contact-enrichment","url":"https://github.com/KhaiStimpson/andrew-crm/pull/58","body":"Implements the contact data enrichment feature end to end, per the design brief in `docs/specs/contact-data-enrichment.md`. External data (company website, news, AU/NZ registries, optional paid person data) enriches contacts through **one ingestion pipeline with three sinks** — all gated by a per-tenant admin opt-in, all sourced, and nothing touches a contact field without human confirmation.\n\n> Consolidates the earlier design-brief PR (#57, now closed) — the brief and its housekeeping are included here, so this is the single PR for the feature.\n\n## What it does\n\n- **Free-first providers** behind a common `IEnrichmentProvider` seam:\n  - `CompanyWebsiteEnrichmentProvider` — OG/meta from the email domain → company, logo, description.\n  - `NewsSignalProvider` — Google News RSS by company, with a headline-match relevance gate.\n  - `AbrAbnProvider` (AU) / `NzbnProvider` (NZ) — official business registries, matched by company name with a conservative confidence gate. **Config-gated** (`Enrichment:Abr:Guid` / `Enrichment:Nzbn:ApiKey`): inert until their credential is set.\n  - `PeopleDataLabsProvider` — optional paid person-level enrichment via a per-tenant **BYO key** (stored DataProtection-encrypted).\n- **Three sinks:** field findings → `EnrichmentSuggestion` (suggest-then-confirm, mirroring `Commitment`); knowledge → `ExternalKnowledge`, a citable AI retrieval source (`AiSourceKind.ExternalKnowledge`); signals → a timeline `Activity` **and** knowledge, with notable ones also becoming a Today-digest `RecommendationKind.EnrichmentSignal`.\n- **Surfaces:** an \"Enrich\" button + review panel on the contact page; signals in the relationship timeline; notable signals in the Today digest; an admin opt-in toggle on both the General and AI-governance settings tabs, plus the BYO-key field.\n- **Automation:** auto-enrich on contact create and CSV/vCard import (Hangfire, gated + bounded); a daily scheduled refresh that re-enriches a bounded, stalest-first slice per tenant.\n- **AI integration:** enriched knowledge flows into the Relationship Brief through the existing PII gateway and is authorized by `AiSourceAuthorizationService`. Selection is factored behind `IExternalKnowledgeSelector` (the RAG seam) so a future vector top-k selector can replace today's bounded recency inclusion without touching treatments.\n\n## Privacy & governance\n\nOff by default; explicit tenant-admin opt-in, re-checked before every fetch; every run audited (`EnrichmentAuditEvent`). Field changes only apply on human accept. External knowledge is tokenised by the PII gateway like any other source. BYO keys are encrypted at rest.\n\n## Testing\n\n~150 enrichment unit tests (parsers, provider mapping, relevance/confidence gates, fail-soft, routing/dedupe, opt-in gating, scheduler selection, RAG seam). Full suite: **307 passing**. The only failures are 4 pre-existing Playwright browser-binary tests, unchanged by this branch. Key flows were also driven end-to-end in the running app (Enrich → accept, timeline signal, Today digest, BYO-key encryption).\n\n## Notes for reviewers\n\n- Dual Sqlite + SqlServer EF migrations included for each schema change.\n- New config keys documented in the README.\n- **NZBN** parser is verified field-by-field against the official OpenAPI spec (`/entities` search: `nzbn`, `entityName`, `entityTypeDescription`, `entityStatusDescription`; `Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key` header) — ready to go live once the key is set.\n- **ABR** is built to the documented JSONP `*.aspx` endpoints (callback param sent, envelope unwrapped); a live smoke is pending the GUID being provisioned, and a small field-name tweak may be needed at first real call.\n- Deferred by design: a per-tenant enrichment spend governor (v1 uses a slow rolling cadence + per-run cap instead) and the vector RAG selector (seam is in place).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","baseSha":"ecf9d53ed2c3b9482a094681cdf501cf2c8c7a0c","headSha":"2baaca76d26ccd0b73159e1e9c11a97dc73c360d","mergeBaseSha":"ecf9d53ed2c3b9482a094681cdf501cf2c8c7a0c","updatedAt":"2026-07-20T03:39:20Z","files":[{"path":".gitignore","additions":1},{"path":"CONTEXT.md","additions":38},{"path":"README.md","additions":2},{"path":"docs/specs/contact-data-enrichment.md","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":200},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Data/AppDbContext.cs","additions":27},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Data/Entities.cs","additions":164,"deletions":1},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719033604_AddContactEnrichment.Designer.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":2472,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"Generated code"},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719033604_AddContactEnrichment.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":200,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"Database migration"},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719034901_AddContactCompanyLogoUrl.Designer.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":2475,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"Generated code"},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719034901_AddContactCompanyLogoUrl.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":28,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"Database migration"},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719082541_AddEnrichmentSignalCount.Designer.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":2478,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"Generated code"},{"path":"src/AndrewCrm.Web/Migrations/SqlServer/20260719082541_AddEnrichmentSignalCount.cs","kind":"FILE_CHANGE_KIND_ADDED","additions":29,"isMechanical":true,"mechanicalReason":"